        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0151" n="51" xml:id="pg51"/>

                <head>No. 36.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kasson to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 18, 1880</date>.
                        (Received March 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 295.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: A telegram from Mr. William Paine, the
                    commercial agent of the United States at Bucharest, addressed to me, was
                    yesterday received at this legation, as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Recognition of Roumania by England, France, Germany, takes place Friday
                            next. Have been asked by minister foreign affairs what our government
                            intends doing. Please instruct me.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">WILLIAM PAINE.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>To this telegram I have replied as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Await instructions from Washington. Are you yet recognized as consular
                            officer?</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">KASSON.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN A. KASSON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
